    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract storage-operations limit policy. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Controls three storage-maintenance axes:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Background jobs</bold> — maximum concurrently running maintenance jobs (index rebuild, GC, WAL archival, etc.).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Compaction rate</bold> — maximum bytes-per-second fed to the compaction engine.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Snapshots</bold> — maximum concurrently active snapshot operations.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Implementations are installed into EditionManager via <computeroutput>EditionManager::installStorageOpsPolicy()</computeroutput> and consulted by the storage engine before scheduling any background operation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
